<!DOCTYPE service-group SYSTEM "avahi-service.dtd">

<!--
  avahi-lwm2m.service — FALLBACK discovery path for the LAB bench.
  Install to: /etc/avahi/services/lwm2m-thingsboard.service

  ONLY use this when `ot-ctl srp client state` answers "Error 35: InvalidCommand",
  i.e. otbr-agent was built without OT_SRP_CLIENT=ON so it cannot register the
  record into its own SRP server. The primary path is
      python tools/lab_tb/lab_tb_srp.py publish
  which puts the record straight in `ot-ctl srp server service`.

  *** NEVER RUN BOTH AT ONCE ***
  The OTBR's Advertising Proxy already mirrors every SRP registration out to
  mDNS. Adding this file on top publishes a SECOND "ThingsBoard-Edge" instance
  on the same link; avahi resolves the collision by renaming ours to
  "ThingsBoard-Edge #2", which no longer matches SRV_INSTANCE_LABEL in
  src/lwm2m_discover.c:24 and breaks discovery in a way that looks like a
  firmware bug.

  HOW THIS REACHES A THREAD NODE
    avahi publishes _lwm2m._udp.local on the infra link (eth0 in WSL); the
    OTBR's *Discovery Proxy* answers the node's query for
    _lwm2m._udp.default.service.arpa. by browsing mDNS and translating the
    names back into the Thread domain. That requires otbr-agent to have been
    built with OTBR_DNSSD_DISCOVERY_PROXY=ON. There is no runtime switch, so
    probe it empirically after installing:
        ot-ctl dns browse _lwm2m._udp.default.service.arpa.
    NXDOMAIN / "Error 25: NotFound" here means the proxy is not compiled in and
    this path cannot work — rebuild otbr-agent, or fix the SRP-client path.

  THE HOST RECORD IS THE OTHER HALF
    <host-name> below points at thingsboard-edge.local, which avahi does not own.
    Its AAAA must be published separately, and it MUST be the wpan0 OMR address
    (not eth0's) or the node will resolve an address it cannot route to. Add it
    to /etc/avahi/hosts and restart avahi-daemon:
        echo "<OMR-address> thingsboard-edge.local" >> /etc/avahi/hosts
        systemctl restart avahi-daemon
    `python tools/lab_tb/lab_tb_srp.py install-avahi` does both steps and fills in
    the OMR address it reads live from ot-ctl.

  The port MUST match the ThingsBoard LwM2M transport bind port. 5683 is not
  negotiable: src/lwm2m_discover.c:22,148 hardcodes it on the host-AAAA path.
-->

<service-group>

  <!-- Service instance label. MUST equal SRV_INSTANCE_LABEL in
       src/lwm2m_discover.c:24. replace-wildcards="no" keeps avahi from
       substituting the machine name into it. -->
  <name replace-wildcards="no">ThingsBoard-Edge</name>

  <service protocol="any">
    <type>_lwm2m._udp</type>
    <port>5683</port>
    <!-- Target of the SRV record. Resolved from /etc/avahi/hosts, which must
         map it to the wpan0 OMR address. -->
    <host-name>thingsboard-edge.local</host-name>
  </service>

</service-group>
